(opcodes and weird facts about those opcodes, the core of it is small. Here is that core. What) Tj
T*
(if a stack, but virtual The bytecode assumes that when it is run, it will be operating on a) Tj
T*
(stack. This means that every opcode has implicit stack inputs and implicit stack outputs. push) Tj
T*
(3 , for example, has empty stack inputs and one stack output. By contrast, add has two stack) Tj
T*
(inputs and one stack output. Some instructions such as nop are empty on both counts. As far as) Tj
